# Authoritative compiler, language and runtime ABI versions.
# tools/gen_version_b.sh generates src/version.b; test/version.sh checks synchronization.
# Release packagers require the tag to match this file.
# Keep the compiler below 1.0.0 until all public 1.0 release gates pass.
compiler=0.1.52
language=1.0

# 22: Native parked cancellation uses cleanup on ELF/Mach-O x86_64/arm64; interpreted host calls return cancellation to the tree walker through shared per-fiber handler, cancellation-state and cleanup-mask entries.
# 21: beans_with_collection_deferred scopes collector/deinit exclusion counters across nesting and contained unwind without changing immediate ARC destruction.
# 20: beans_json_decode_probe_publish and beans_json_decode_probe replace the encoding bridge's shared probe with per-thread status, error code, offset/record count and field index storage.
# ABI 20: Typed decoding passes the publish callback in req[4], probe values in req[5..7] and existing callbacks in req[8..11]; runtime TLS keeps the encoding bridge libc-only, with a single-thread freestanding fallback.
# ABI 20: The hosted beans_json_decode_probe replaces beans_enc_json_decode_probe; the interpreter returns zeros because it does not lower typed JSON decoding.
# 19: permessage-deflate adds beans_ws_valid_utf8 for inflated text, negotiated compression in beans_ws_new req[2], reserved bits in beans_ws_queue req[2] and window bits (0 or 9..15) in beans_zlib_stream_new req[3].
# ABI 19: WebSocket message events use a 10-byte [u8 opcode][u8 rsv][u64 len] header before the payload.
# 18: beans_contained_enter/leave/caught track per-fiber catch frames and recover a panic at the call site's forced-unwind landing pad; enter promotes a root thread to a worker when needed.
# ABI 18: Panics unwind on brewed fibers or fibers with a catch frame; an uncontained root-fiber panic still exits with status 3.
# 17: beans_net_send_pair_wait sends two buffers from a concatenation offset using sendmsg with MSG_NOSIGNAL or WSASend, allowing short-write retries without allocation.
# ABI 17: beans_rt_host_invoke calls hosted entries in-process with typed word conversion, returning 1 for success, 0 for an unhosted name and -1 for a declaration mismatch; hosted rows expose both address and call entry points.
# ABI 17: beans_net_send_pair_text reads string length with beans_slen and reuses the pair-send engine; older interpreters join the buffers before sending equivalent bytes.
# ABI 17: beans_bytes_reserve_raw supplies json.encode_into req[6] with a void* callback that sets Bytes length/capacity and returns backing storage; the interpreter uses its own append path.
# ABI 17: beans_alloc_bytes skips recycled pooled-payload zeroing for callers that overwrite the complete buffer; large allocations remain zeroed and hosted rows support address lookup and invocation.
# 16: Order kind 7 compares loaded tags for payload-free enum slots; slot_cmp traps unknown kinds to detect compiler/runtime mismatches.
# 15: beans_term_is_tty/size/set_raw/restore expose portable terminal control in the full runtime profile, returning 0 or a negative status (-errno on POSIX, -1000 when unsupported) with size written to caller storage.
# 14: List iteration detects structural changes through beans_list_iter_invalid and the change_count/change_kind words at offsets 40/44 of the unchanged 48-byte BList.
# ABI 14: All structural list operations update invalidation state; sort_by_key and its decv/val variants invoke the key function once for a single-element list.
# 13: beans_str_width and beans_width_utf8 share column-width measurement; beans_show_map_iter, beans_show_enter/beans_show_push_leave and beans_list_join_wide add cycle-safe derived rendering of maps, results, structs, classes and wide list elements.
# 12: beans_fiber_unwind_finish ends brewed fibers after defers and drops; beans_fiber_begin_unwind/unwinding/message manage platform unwinding and double-panic reports, while unsupported targets retain abandonment.
# 11: beans_fiber_* and beans_brew* add fiber scheduling, cancellation, joins and scoped joins; beans_chan_try_send/recv and their typed variants add nonblocking channel operations.
# 10: Removing async/await also removes beans_task_slot/beans_set_task_slot and the beans_reactor_* parked-readiness registry.
# 9: Resolved reflection method, initializer and function handles avoid repeated name resolution through their call_handle entries.
# 8: beans_poll_wait_into fills a caller-owned event buffer.
# 7: Adds Bytes.filled, Bytes.append_int_text and Thread.detach.
# 6: Adds per-thread runtime-hook guard entry points.
runtime_abi=22
